        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The monoglyceride process reacts raw oil triglycerides directly with additional glycerol at high temperatures (~240°C) using an alkaline catalyst to break the oil down into mono- and di-glycerides, which are then esterified with phthalic anhydride. The fatty acid process uses pre-isolated pure fatty acids directly reacted with polyols and dibasic acids in a single step. The fatty acid process offers superior control over molecular weight distribution and final resin properties, but at a higher raw material cost."
      }
